This one isn't an ARexx nor MCI trick or anything, it's just a simple
little textfile that I thought some would get some benefit out of...

It seems there is always someone confused by voting topics that use
floats so I wrote up a little how-to if you will that seems to clear
the mystery.  The only problem is I cannot find any possible way of
having this added automatically (no way to test whether a vote topic
uses floats or not), so you have to add this manually.  [sigh]  Much
easier than answering mail about it or watching several people put
1 float on one item and then having them ask you why the topic keeps
popping up...  :)

Once you've finished writing the text for the voting topic, directly
on the next line -- DON'T SKIP A LINE -- type:

{*0PFiles:FloatVote}

The above { is actually a control-Q commands and remember to modify the
path to where you placed the "FloatVote" textfile.
